[size=5][b]Blender to the native Rust client — custom asset experiments[/b][/size]

Hi everyone! We have also been experimenting with an AI-assisted authoring workbench for original RuneScape-inspired 3D assets. The useful test is how a model looks and moves in the native Rust client, so Blender beauty renders and native results are kept separate.

[b]The first conversion proof[/b]

An early procedural arch went from an editable Blender scene into the native model format, then into an isolated live world. The lighting changes between the Blender and native images are real; conversion does not carry Blender’s whole material system with it.

[i]Blender render — The first procedural Cinderworks arch, shown in Blender studio lighting.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/custom-models/01-first-blender.png[/img]

[i]Prepared native render — The same original arch after conversion, through the native software renderer.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/custom-models/02-first-native.png[/img]

[i]Live native gameplay — The original arch placed in an isolated live Rust client/server test.[/i]
